insert into public.budget_of_work (grade, subject, content_markdown, source_file)
values (
  6,
  'Science',
  $bow$# Grade 6 Science — Budget of Work

## Term 1 (Q1: Matter — Changes and Properties)
Wk1-2: Investigating physical changes in materials (change in size, shape, state) and identifying them as reversible | Wk3-4: Investigating chemical changes (rusting, burning, souring) and identifying them as producing new substances | Wk5-6: Differentiating physical from chemical changes through guided experiments | Wk7-8: Describing factors that speed up or slow down chemical changes (heat, exposure to air, catalysts in everyday contexts) | Wk9-10: Applying knowledge of physical and chemical changes to explain everyday phenomena (food spoilage, cooking, rusting of tools) in a term project.

**Special Science enrichment:** Have the learner run a real, safe controlled comparison at home (e.g., two identical pieces of fruit, one exposed to air and one covered) and record daily observations to conclude which factor caused the difference.

## Term 2 (Q2: Living Things — Heredity and Ecosystems)
Wk1-2: Describing how traits are passed from parents to offspring in plants and animals (basic heredity concepts) | Wk3-4: Differentiating inherited traits from traits acquired through environment or habit | Wk5-6: Describing the interdependence of organisms within an ecosystem (producers, consumers, decomposers) | Wk7-8: Explaining the effects of human activity on the balance of an ecosystem | Wk9-10: Proposing ways to protect and restore ecosystems in the local community, as a term project.

**Special Science enrichment:** Have the learner observe and record real inherited vs. environmentally-influenced traits within their own family or a local plant/animal example, and explain which category each observed trait falls into and why.

## Term 3 (Q3: Force, Motion, and Energy — Simple Circuits and Machines)
Wk1-2: Describing series and parallel circuits and their differences | Wk3-4: Investigating how simple machines combine to form compound machines, and how this affects the work done | Wk5-6: Describing forms of energy (mechanical, electrical, heat, light) and simple energy transformations in everyday devices | Wk7-8: Explaining the importance of energy conservation and safe use of electrical devices | Wk9-10: Designing and explaining a simple working model (a circuit or compound machine) as a term project.

**Special Science enrichment:** Require the term project model to go through at least one real design iteration — build, test, identify a specific failure, and explain the exact change made to fix it, documented with before/after notes.

## Term 4 (Q4: Earth and Space — Solar System and Climate)
Wk1-2: Describing the Sun, planets, and other members of the solar system and their relative positions | Wk3-4: Explaining day and night, and the seasons, in terms of Earth's rotation and revolution | Wk5-6: Differentiating weather from climate, and describing the climate types found in the Philippines | Wk7-8: Explaining the causes and effects of climate change, and its impact on the Philippines | Wk9-10: Year-end integration — proposing and explaining a personal or community action to address climate change, drawing on knowledge from matter, living things, energy, and Earth/space across the year.

**Special Science enrichment:** Have the learner research one real, local example of a climate-related impact in their own community (flooding, drought, changed harvest timing) and connect it explicitly to a specific climate-change cause discussed in class.$bow$,
  'https://www.deped.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/MATATAG-Science-CG-Grade-4-and-7.pdf'
);
